"# Finding TECH-023
2 different pages all declare https://www.example.com/ as their canonical

Site: https://www.example.com/
Framework: react_spa

## What a correct fix looks like
Many pages declare the same canonical URL, so each claims to be a copy of one page. Every page must declare its own URL. Usually one static tag in the HTML shell or a default value in a shared head component is the cause: make it derive from the current route, and remove any static tag that would otherwise win.

## How we will know the fix failed
Re-fetch two of the pages; if each names itself, this was wrong.

## What the audit observed
{"kind":"markup","url":"https://www.example.com/about","locator":"link[rel=\\"canonical\\"]","snippet":"<link rel=\\"canonical\\" href=\\"https://www.example.com/\\">","observedAt":"2026-10-05T00:00:00.000Z","source":"crawler"}

## Affected pages (2)
- https://www.example.com/about
- https://www.example.com/contact

## Libraries the project already depends on
react, react-helmet-async

## Files you may edit, shown in full
### index.html
<<<FILE
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Example Safaris</title>
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://www.example.com/" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="root"></div>
  </body>
</html>

FILE>>>

